    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Retires a live suggestion-generation path + changes the SSE `suggestions` wire contract on the shared chat surface (hot-path BFF + ADR-039 grounded-proposer boundary); requires code-review + adr-check.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Architectural: retires the ungrounded generator, generalizes the grounded proposer to a new trigger moment, and reshapes the suggestion wire contract on ChatEndpoints (hot-path). ADR-039 closed-catalog-proposer fidelity is the load-bearing constraint.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>Wave2-E2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits ChatEndpoints.cs (hot-path BFF) + AssistantSuggestionService + the SSE suggestions contract; coordinate with 021b (client render) + compose-r5/r6; run /conflict-check before the PR.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>012</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ai, spaarkeai</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-9 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Make every rendered follow-on suggestion capability-backed OR a safe conversational question, by consolidating onto the GROUNDED PROPOSER pattern already shipped in `AssistantSuggestionService`. (1) RETIRE the ungrounded free-string generator (`ChatEndpoints.GenerateAndEmitSuggestionsAsync`) and stop emitting the untyped `suggestions: string[]` SSE event. (2) GENERALIZE the grounded proposer so it runs after a chat response — keyed off the conversation tail + the deterministically context-scoped candidate capability menu (union of open-tab context-types + session/host) + the active tab's server-derived content — and returns a TYPED list of ≤3 suggestions of two kinds: `capability` (carries a real `targetBindingId` the model SELECTED from the supplied menu — hallucinated ids dropped, exactly as `ParseSuggestions` already does) and `question` (free text that re-enters the grounded agent loop, safe by construction). (3) Make CADENCE predictable: one grounded pass per assistant turn; absence means "nothing relevant", never a timeout/short-ack/keyword-hijack artifact. The model authors labels + question text (full creativity); it NEVER authors a capability's routing target. Follow notes/021-grounded-suggestions-design-delta.md.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE BFF developer. Deep familiarity with the ADR-039 closed-catalog grounded-proposer pattern (AssistantSuggestionService), the Linear AI Consumer primitives (IActionResolver/IActionRunner), the SUGGEST-FOLLOWUPS catalog Action, the SprkChat SSE contract, and the deterministic context pre-filter (open-tab context-types, active-tab visible state).</role>
  <goal>Every follow-on suggestion the Assistant emits is either a capability chip carrying a real, selected `targetBindingId` or a safe conversational question; the ungrounded free-string generator is gone; suggestions are emitted as a typed two-kind SSE structure; cadence is one predictable grounded pass per turn (no dead-ends possible, no random silence).</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Per the FR-04 design delta (notes/021-grounded-suggestions-design-delta.md, owner-approved 2026-08-17): the dead-end problem is the ungrounded `GenerateAndEmitSuggestionsAsync` (ChatEndpoints.cs ~:3211) — a ~100-output-token LLM call fed only the last user message + 500 chars of the response, NEVER told what the system can do, emitting untyped free strings. The FIX already exists as `AssistantSuggestionService.SuggestAsync` (the grounded proposer for the proactive-tab moment): it hands the model the REAL context-scoped candidate menu WITH descriptions and DROPS any suggestion whose id is not a supplied candidate (ParseSuggestions closed-catalog guard). This task generalizes that proposer to the after-a-response moment and retires the ungrounded path. TWO honest kinds: capability (bindingId → dispatch via the existing Click path) and question (text → re-enters the loop, grounded-outcomes-safe). Cadence today is inconsistent because of THREE hidden skips in ChatEndpoints (`:977` keyword action-chip hijack; `:1002` <150-char dedup-ack skip; 2s timeout) plus a separate proactive trigger — replace with one predictable pass. The code's own R7 comment (ChatEndpoints.cs:990-998) already prescribes this direction. Input context must be GENEROUS (conversation tail + real menu + descriptions + active-tab state); output stays modest + structured (~400 tokens for the ≤3 typed items). Active-tab identity + open-tab awareness already flow (activeContextTabId + liveTabs → context pre-filter, task 030). The three deterministic `[action:upload/search/select]` chips stay as-is for now (deterministic + backed); folding them into the grounded menu is a deferred phase-2.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/AssistantSuggestionService.cs (the grounded proposer to generalize — candidate menu + descriptions + closed-catalog ParseSuggestions guard)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/ChatEndpoints.cs (retire GenerateAndEmitSuggestionsAsync ~:3211; the after-response suggestion emit ~:963-1021; the SSE suggestions event ~:3268)</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/actions/suggest-followups.action.json (the SUGGEST-FOLLOWUPS Action prompt+schema — author the two-kind output + the capability-vs-question split instruction + label grammar; mirror the operand shape)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/ConsumerRoutingService.cs (ListTextProjectableBindingsAsync + FilterByContextType — the deterministic candidate pre-filter to scope by open-tab context-types + session/host)</file>
      <file>the SSE event models (ChatSseEvent / ChatSseSuggestionsData) — evolve suggestions: string[] → a typed two-kind array (version carefully)</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ + tests/integration/seam/** (grounded-proposer selection + closed-catalog-guard + typed-output + cadence tests)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039" scope="the proposer">The suggestion turn is a PROPOSER, not a decider: it selects ≤3 from the deterministically pre-filtered closed candidate set; a suggestion whose capability id is not a supplied candidate MUST be dropped (no uncataloged capability may be proposed). No classifier, no second dispatch surface. The one probabilistic decider stays the Text-path agent turn; suggestion chips ride the existing Click path on click.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-040" scope="the proposer">The suggestion turn consumes no tool reads and persists nothing (ephemeral UI) — store-before-render is vacuously satisfied; do NOT add a new store.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015" scope="grounded input">Active-tab content passed to the model stays server-derived + bounded (the same compact visible-state shape the chat turn uses); never trust client bytes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="no dead-ends">A rendered capability suggestion MUST carry a real selected targetBindingId; a question suggestion re-enters the grounded loop (safe). MUST NOT emit an untyped free string with no backing. MUST NOT use a keyword heuristic to classify suggestions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="BFF §10" scope="every BFF-touching change">Publish size ≤60 MB compressed (baseline 44.96 MB incl. PDBs) — measure + report absolute + delta; no new HIGH CVE; add/update tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (NFR-08).</constraint>
    <constraint source="wire-contract" scope="SSE suggestions">Evolve the suggestions SSE event to the typed two-kind shape deliberately; coordinate the exact shape with 021b BEFORE landing (a client that expects string[] must not break).</constraint>
  </constraints>
