  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Study AssistantSuggestionService (candidate menu build + BuildInput operand + ParseSuggestions closed-catalog guard) and the after-response suggestion emit path in ChatEndpoints (the three skips + the SSE event).</step>
    <step order="2">Generalize the grounded proposer to the conversational moment: add a conversation-tail input + scope the candidate menu by the union of open-tab context-types + session/host (reuse the deterministic pre-filter); ground labels in the active tab's server-derived content.</step>
    <step order="3">Author the SUGGEST-FOLLOWUPS Action for the TWO-KIND typed output (capability {targetBindingId,label} + question {text}) with the split instruction + label grammar (imperative+capability vs interrogative+question); keep the closed-catalog id-drop guard.</step>
    <step order="4">Retire GenerateAndEmitSuggestionsAsync; wire the after-response path to the grounded proposer; make cadence one predictable pass (remove the coupling to the <150-char skip so a post-capability short ack still gets grounded followups).</step>
    <step order="5">Evolve the SSE suggestions event to the typed two-kind shape (coordinate with 021b); keep it best-effort (ADR-019 — silent skip on failure, never break the turn).</step>
    <step order="6">Tests: the proposer selects only supplied candidate ids (hallucinated dropped); typed two-kind output parses; a question kind round-trips; cadence — a post-capability short-ack turn still yields grounded followups; no untyped free string is emitted. dotnet build + publish size (absolute + delta) + CVE scan.</step>
    <step order="7">/conflict-check before the PR; update TASK-INDEX.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If generalizing the candidate scope to the conversational moment cannot be expressed as the existing deterministic context pre-filter (open-tab context-types + session/host) and appears to need intent detection or a ranker, STOP and escalate (ADR-039 forbids a second decider) rather than adding classification.</trigger>
    <trigger>If retiring the ungrounded generator would leave a real consumer with no grounded equivalent for a needed follow-on, surface it (the grounded proposer + the sprk_chiptransitions ConsumerChips should cover it; a gap is an escalation, not a silent regression).</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>AssistantSuggestionService already IS the closed-catalog grounded proposer (candidate menu + descriptions + hallucinated-id drop); ConsumerChips (sprk_chiptransitions) are the deterministic action-declared followups.</existing>
    <extension>Generalize the existing proposer to the after-response moment + add a typed question kind + retire the ungrounded generator — no new service, no new dispatch surface, no new store (§11); the net change REMOVES a fragile surface.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The ungrounded generator keeps emitting untyped free strings the client cannot verify — the P2 dead-end persists, and cadence stays random (three hidden skips).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/AssistantSuggestionService.cs (generalized to the conversational moment + typed two-kind output)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/ChatEndpoints.cs (ungrounded generator retired; grounded proposer wired to the after-response path; predictable cadence)</output>
    <output type="code">infra/dataverse/actions/suggest-followups.action.json (two-kind output schema + split instruction + label grammar)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ + tests/integration/seam/** (proposer selection, closed-catalog guard, typed output, cadence)</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The ungrounded free-string generator (GenerateAndEmitSuggestionsAsync) is removed; no untyped suggestions: string[] SSE event is emitted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every capability suggestion carries a targetBindingId that is one of the supplied candidates (a hallucinated/off-catalog id is dropped) — negative case tested.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The proposer emits a typed two-kind structure (capability + question); a question kind is a safe conversational follow-on (no bindingId).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cadence is one predictable grounded pass per turn: a post-capability short-ack turn still yields grounded followups (the pre-existing <150-char silence is gone).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No classifier / second dispatch surface is added (verified against ADR-039 MUST-NOTs); the candidate scope is the deterministic context pre-filter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish ≤60 MB reported (absolute + delta); no new HIGH CVE; tests added/updated.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Coordinate the exact typed SSE shape with 021b (client). The three deterministic [action:*] chips stay for now; folding them into the grounded menu is a deferred phase-2. The after-capability-dispatch moment may lean on the existing sprk_chiptransitions ConsumerChips (deterministic action-declared followups — task 023 territory); reconcile whether those merge with the grounded proposer's output or stay the dispatch-turn source. /conflict-check with compose-r5/r6 before the PR.</notes>
